inhomogeneousSystemOfParameters -- generates an inhomogeneous system of parameters
**********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        inhomogeneousSystemOfParameters(I,A)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,
      * A, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Attempts => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 100,
        number of attempts made to generate an inhomogeneous system of
        parameters
      * Bound => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 1, bound on
        the value of the random coefficients
      * Sparseness => a *note real number: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,, default value .5,
        between 0 and 1 giving the frequency of the coefficients being equal to
        zero
      * Maximal => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        true, whether to insist on searching for a maximal inhomogeneous system
        of parameters
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,

Description
===========

Given a ring and an ideal, inhomogeneousSystemOfParameters attempts to generate
an inhomogeneous system of parameters contained in I. The algorithm is based on
one found in Chapter 5.5 of W. Vasconcelos' book: Computational Methods in
Commutative Algebra and Algebraic Geometry.
+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = ZZ/5051[x, y, z];                   |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal (x, x*y, y*z);                |
|                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of A                              |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : X = inhomogeneousSystemOfParameters(I,A)|
|                                             |
|o3 = | yz+x xy |                             |
|                                             |
|             1      2                        |
|o3 : Matrix A  <-- A                         |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isRegularSequence(X,A)                  |
|                                             |
|o4 = true                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
Here are examples with optional inputs:
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : A = ZZ/5051[x, y, z];                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : I = ideal (x, x*y, y*z);                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : Ideal of A                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : inhomogeneousSystemOfParameters(I,A,Attempts=>1,Bound=>100,Sparseness   |
|--warning: no maximal regular sequence found                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = 0                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|             1                                                               |
|o7 : Matrix A  <-- 0                                                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|=>.9)                                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
Here are examples with the optional input Maximal => false:
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : x = symbol x; y = symbol y;                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : n = 2;                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : A = ZZ/101[x_(1,1)..x_(n,n),y_(1,1)..y_(n,n)];                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : X = transpose genericMatrix(A,n,n);                                    |
|                                                                             |
|              2      2                                                       |
|o12 : Matrix A  <-- A                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : Y = transpose genericMatrix(A,y_(1,1),n,n);                            |
|                                                                             |
|              2      2                                                       |
|o13 : Matrix A  <-- A                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : b = ideal(X*Y - Y*X);                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o14 : Ideal of A                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : B = A/b;                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : inhomogeneousSystemOfParameters(B,Attempts=>1,Maximal=>false)          |
|                                                                             |
|o16 = | -x_(2,1)-y_(1,2)+y_(2,1) x_(1,2)-y_(2,2)                             |
|      -----------------------------------------------------------------------|
|      -x_(2,1)+x_(2,2)-y_(1,1)+y_(1,2) -x_(1,1)+x_(2,1)                      |
|      -----------------------------------------------------------------------|
|      x_(1,1)-x_(2,1)-y_(1,1) x_(1,1)+x_(1,2) |                              |
|                                                                             |
|              1      6                                                       |
|o16 : Matrix B  <-- B                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

This symbol is provided by the package *note Depth: Top,.

