isCM -- whether a ring or module is Cohen-Macaulay
**************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isCM(A)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note Ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring, or *note Module:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Module,
  * Outputs:
      * *note Boolean: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,

Description
===========

This command merely checks if the depth of A equals the Krull dimension of A.
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = ZZ/2[x,y,z];                                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isCM(A)                                                         |
|                                                                     |
|o2 = true                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : A = ZZ/2[x,y]/(x^2,x*y);                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isCM(A)                                                         |
|                                                                     |
|o4 = false                                                           |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : A =  ZZ/101[a_1,a_2,b_1,b_2,c_1]/ideal(a_1*b_1,a_2*b_2,b_1*c_1);|
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isCM(A)                                                         |
|                                                                     |
|o6 = false                                                           |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

This symbol is provided by the package *note Depth: Top,.

Caveat
======

Typically when one thinks of a Cohen-Macaulay ring or module, one is in the
local case. Since the local case is not yet implemented into Macaulay 2, we
compute over the ideal generated by by *note generators(Ring):
(Macaulay2Doc)generators_lpRing_rp,.

Ways to use isCM:
=================

  * "isCM(Module)"
  * "isCM(Ring)"

