isRegularSequence -- whether a list is regular over a ring or module
********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isRegularSequence(X,A) or isRegularSequence(X) 
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, or *note Matrix:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,
      * A, a *note Ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring, or *note Module:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Module,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,

Description
===========

Given a list X, the function isRegularSequence tells if X forms a regular
sequence. If X consists of homogeneous elements, it does this by comparing the
Hilbert series of A and the Hilbert series of A/XA. Otherwise it checks the
injectivity of the maps defined by multiplication by the elements of X and also
checks if XA = A.
+--------------------------------+
|i1 : A = ZZ/2[x, y, z];         |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : X1 = {x, y*(x-1), z*(x-1)};|
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : isRegularSequence X1       |
|                                |
|o3 = true                       |
+--------------------------------+
|i4 : X2 = {z*(x-1), y*(x-1), x};|
+--------------------------------+
|i5 : isRegularSequence X2       |
|                                |
|o5 = false                      |
+--------------------------------+
|i6 : X3 = {1_A, x, y};          |
+--------------------------------+
|i7 : isRegularSequence X3       |
|                                |
|o7 = false                      |
+--------------------------------+

This symbol is provided by the package *note Depth: Top,.

