regularSequenceCheck -- how much of a list is regular
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        regularSequenceCheck(X,A)
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, or *note Matrix:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,
      * A, a *note Ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring, or *note Module:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Module,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,

Description
===========

Given a list X, the function regularSequenceCheck gives an integer indicating
how many initial elements of a List form a regular sequence.
+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = ZZ[x_1..x_4]/(x_4^2)               |
|                                            |
|o1 = A                                      |
|                                            |
|o1 : QuotientRing                           |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : regularSequenceCheck({x_1..x_4},A)     |
|                                            |
|o2 = 3                                      |
+--------------------------------------------+

This symbol is provided by the package *note Depth: Top,.

Caveat
======

regularSequenceCheck merely checks the injectivity of the maps in question. It
does not check to see if XA = A.

